In the non-relativistic limit where $|\mathbf{v}| \ll c$, the spatial components reduce to Newtonian force $\mathbf{F} = m \mathbf{a}$ and the temporal component matches the standard work-energy relation $\frac{dE}{dt} = \mathbf{F} \cdot \mathbf{v}$. For variable-mass systems (such as emitting rockets or decaying particles), $\frac{dm}{d\tau} 
eq 0$, and the orthogonality condition generalizes to $K^\mu U_\mu = -c^2 \frac{dm}{d\tau} 
eq 0$.
